       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose this high risks hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the original dose, please confirm it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
